        "chapterNumber": "Chapter I (Cont.) ♡",
        "chapterTitle": "A Sign & Classroom BTF-11",
        "dateOrLocation": "11 April",
        "decorativeInitial": "",
        "storyParagraphs": [
          "I'm someone who believes in God. For every decision I take, I usually ask Him, myself, and my parents before going ahead. And this time was no different.",
          "I told Him that if I happened to see you again coincidentally, without looking for you or hunting for you, only then would I try to know more about you. Otherwise, nothing.",
          "And I left it at that.",
          "Within two days, I was standing on the ground floor of B-Block, revising for my lab IA in the morning. I just turned to the other side and saw you walking alone wearing a red dress .",
          "I was so confused, not knowing what to do. Should I follow you to find out which class you were in, or should I just leave it? I thought about it a couple of times and then decided, yes.",
          "I ran upstairs looking for you, but I couldn't find you anywhere. Still, I kept walking ahead, and then I saw you. You had just entered your classroom, BTF-11. You were wearing a red dress.",
          "And after that, life completely changed;",
          "I was someone who used to think only about how satellites revolve around planets. Suddenly, I started thinking about how I could get to know you and talk to you.",
          "You suddenly became the centre of gravity for my satellite system.",
          "I was new to this business: I had absolutely no idea where to begin, how to begin, or what to do.",
          "And that's how I eventually ended up speaking with you.",
          "Whenever I think about you, this song somehow starts playing in my mind. [[music:m_1794341020222]]"
        ],
